0.1.1 (2026-11-25)
  * The red-cyan sentence on the page says what each kind sees, without ranking the outputs (queue row 68; the
    edition's recorded line of 2026-10-07: red-cyan is a first-class output, spoken of with respect): protan and deutan, "With red-cyan glasses, 3D
    pictures keep all their depth for you, and fewer of their colours stay apart: the glasses rebuild the colours from red
    and cyan, and red and green already run together for you. A 3D television or another of the screen's 3D outputs
    keeps every colour."; monochromacy, "With red-cyan glasses you see 3D pictures with all their depth, as anyone does:
    each eye gets its own picture through its lens, and the colours play no part."; tritan, none (the study measured the
    lenses apart, 71.5, not the colours of a 3D picture). Ten languages; the Korean sentence no longer speaks as "me".
  * A variant's texts read at 4.5:1 in unfocused windows too: the helper carries a port of KColorScheme's inactive rules
    (the [ColorEffects:Inactive] effects and the selected row drawn from the Window set; KColorUtils' arithmetic), equal
    to KColorScheme's own colours within one level on 1440 colours of the edition's looks.
  * The shipped variants of Sparky Stereo Oxygen Dark and data/limits.json are made again from the edition's looks as
    fixed in sparky-stereo-look 20261125.1 and sparky-stereo-look-kubabbar-glass 20261125; Sparky Stereo Oxygen is measured.

0.1.0 (2026-11-25)
  * First build (queue row 68): System Settings' Colour Vision page beside Accessibility, one choice (none, protan, deutan,
    tritan, monochromacy) and a box for the terminals. It sets KWin's colour correction through the keys KDE's Accessibility
    page uses, the colour-vision variant of the person's colour scheme, Konsole's default profile (a profile of ours whose
    parent is the person's), nano's colours when the person has no nano settings file, and the line the text console's
    login reads. The person's own files are kept and their colours come back exactly at None; what could not be set is said
    on the page. The maps are the accessibility study's of 2026-10-14 (section 1.3), corrected per kind by measurement.
